cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SimForge, please cite it as below."
title: "SimForge"
type: software
version: "0.1.0a1"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jesus010801/simforge"
url: "https://github.com/Jesus010801/simforge"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  SimForge is a Python tool for declarative construction, validation, and
  provenance tracking of GROMACS molecular-simulation systems. It compiles a
  single system specification into reproducible topologies and coordinates,
  gates them with a blocking grompp check, and records SHA256-hashed inputs and
  outputs alongside environment and version metadata.
keywords:
  - molecular-dynamics
  - GROMACS
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - computational-biology
  - molecular-simulation
authors:
